=============================

FFmpeg
------
Beacon requires FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org) to decode and encode video and
audio: it links FFmpeg's libraries (libavformat, libavcodec, libavutil,
libswscale, libswresample) and runs the ffmpeg command-line tool. FFmpeg is
not bundled with Beacon; it must be installed separately by the user.

FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL) version
2.1 or later; builds with optional GPL components, such as Homebrew's, are
under the GNU General Public License (GPL) version 2 or later. Copies of the
licenses are available at:
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html
https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html

FFmpeg source code is available at: https://git.ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.git

whisper.cpp
-----------
Beacon runs whisper.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp) for local
transcripts. It is not bundled with Beacon; it must be installed separately
by the user. whisper.cpp is licensed under the MIT License. The Whisper model
weights it reads, downloaded separately, are released by OpenAI under the MIT
License.

